# The suite's own set: the root one, minus the check doctest defeats.
InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access

# bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
#   230 findings, all of one shape:
#
#       auto object = ub::Object::New(fixture.context);
#       REQUIRE(object.has_value());
#       ... object->Set(...)
#
#   `REQUIRE` aborts the case when it fails, so the access below it is checked -
#   but the check models `std::optional` and not doctest, sees a macro it cannot
#   reason about, and reports every dereference in the suite. The alternative is
#   rewriting several hundred assertions into a form that satisfies a dataflow
#   analysis rather than a reader, which is a worse suite.
#
#   Off for `tests/` alone. The same check over the library's own sources - where
#   every one of these operations returns an optional and an unchecked one really
#   would be a bug - stays on.
